    "description": "Collection of five antique and vintage silver serving utensils featuring a pierced serving fork, three serving spoons of varying shapes and sizes, and a decorative shell-shaped serving spoon.\n\nFour pieces are stamped “STERLING,” while the larger flat-handled serving spoon features multiple historical hallmarks appearing consistent with antique Irish sterling silver. Exact maker and date have not been confirmed.\n\nSeveral pieces feature engraved monograms or decorative initials. The shell-shaped spoon features an ornate floral handle with beaded edging and an engraved “1899” inscription.\n\nTotal weight: Approximately 478 grams, as shown on the digital scale, with the bowl apparently tared.\n\nCondition: Pre-owned antique and vintage condition with visible tarnishing, surface scratches, discoloration, and general wear consistent with age and use. Some markings exhibit wear. Please review all photographs for details of markings, engravings, and overall condition.\nAll five pieces are included. Sold together as pictured.",
